1
00:00:00,226 --> 00:00:04,756
(Q21（单选）) Holly: Hello Dr Green – I’m here to talk to you about my work placement。

2
00:00:04,756 --> 00:00:07,020
Tutor: Oh yes, it’s Holly, isn’t it?

3
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:08,060
Holly: Yes. Holly：

4
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:10,690
Tutor: So, which work placement have you chosen?

5
00:00:10,690 --> 00:00:21,789
Holly: I decided to go for the Orion Stadium placement. The event I’ll be managing is one where I’m helping to set up a sports competition for primary school children.&nbsp;

6
00:00:21,789 --> 00:00:27,895
Tutor: Yup. That’s always a popular placement – even though it can be tougher than you think working with children.

7
00:00:27,895 --> 00:00:36,929
[Q21答案句B： fresh air = outdoors] Holly: I know, but it’s the fresh air that attracts me – organising something indoors doesn’t have the same appeal, even though it might be fun.&nbsp;

8
00:00:36,929 --> 00:00:42,704
(Q22) Tutor: OK, so obviously safety’s going to be one of your key concerns for this event.

9
00:00:42,704 --> 00:00:49,361
Holly: Yes, I’ve already thought about that. I’ll need to make sure none of the equipment’s damaged.&nbsp;

10
00:00:49,361 --> 00:00:59,319
Tutor: Ah well, you’ll be working with schools, so the equipment will be their responsibility. However, the grounds and what goes on there will be yours.

11
00:00:59,319 --> 00:01:06,906
Holly: Oh I see – that’ll include keeping everyone within the boundary once they’re in their kit and on the field?&nbsp;

12
00:01:06,906 --> 00:01:17,252
[Q22答案句C： but your main priority] Tutor: Exactly – you’ll need to inspect areas like changing rooms as well for anything someone can trip over, but your main priority will be not to lose anyone!

13
00:01:17,252 --> 00:01:21,460
Holly: Right. I’ll need staff to help with that.&nbsp;

14
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:23,996
(Q23) Tutor: And don’t forget about the spectators.

15
00:01:23,996 --> 00:01:29,271
Holly: Mmm. I was thinking that many of them will be parents, who could help run the event.&nbsp;

16
00:01:29,271 --> 00:01:34,863
Tutor: I wouldn’t rely on that. They’ll be more interested in filming their children than volunteering.

17
00:01:34,863 --> 00:01:38,719
Holly: I’ll need to make sure they don’t interfere with events doing that!&nbsp;

18
00:01:38,719 --> 00:01:47,222
[Q23答案句A： 解释型] Tutor: And that’s not always easy, especially when a proud parent’s trying to get a snap of their child and you want them to move elsewhere.

19
00:01:47,222 --> 00:01:51,059
(Q24) Holly: OK. What about the scheduling?&nbsp;

20
00:01:51,059 --> 00:02:01,855
Tutor: With sporting events there are all sorts of things that can alter the timetable – like rain, for instance – though so far, we’ve always been lucky with that.

21
00:02:01,855 --> 00:02:10,657
[Q24答案句B] Holly: Yeah, and I was thinking about what to do if someone got hurt as well. I know that last year that caused a terrible delay.&nbsp;

22
00:02:10,657 --> 00:02:13,402
Tutor: You have to be prepared for such things.

23
00:02:13,402 --> 00:02:20,435
Holly: Oh. What if a match ends in a draw – do you let the teams keep going until someone wins?&nbsp;

24
00:02:20,435 --> 00:02:24,549
Tutor: That’ll be up to you – and again, you need to plan for it.

25
00:02:24,549 --> 00:02:26,753
Holly: Right.&nbsp;

26
00:02:26,753 --> 00:02:37,332
(Q25（matching）) Tutor: Now, the aim of your work placement is to give you the opportunity to develop the skills that an events manager needs. So, let’s talk about those a bit.

27
00:02:37,332 --> 00:02:46,325
Holly: Well, I think my communication skills are pretty good. I can talk on the phone to people and book venues and that kind of thing.&nbsp;

28
00:02:46,325 --> 00:02:55,972
Tutor: Good – just remember it isn’t only about what you say. If you meet someone face-to-face and want to persuade them to be a sponsor, for example …

29
00:02:55,972 --> 00:02:59,457
[Q25答案句C： 穿着方面 = appearance] Holly: Oh, I’ll dress up for that! Sure.&nbsp;

30
00:02:59,457 --> 00:03:09,701
(Q26) Tutor: Good. Let’s go on to think about your organisational skills. You’re working in a very people-based industry and that means things won’t always go to plan.

31
00:03:09,701 --> 00:03:13,415
[Q26答案句A： 做好准备make changes = being flexible] Holly: I guess it’s being prepared to make changes that matters.&nbsp;

32
00:03:13,415 --> 00:03:20,496
Tutor: That’s right. You may have to make an on-the-spot change to a timetable because of a problem you hadn’t anticipated …

33
00:03:20,496 --> 00:03:22,839
Holly: … just do it! OK.&nbsp;

34
00:03:22,839 --> 00:03:25,545
(Q27) Tutor: How’s your time management these days?

35
00:03:25,545 --> 00:03:32,224
Holly: I’m working on it – I’m certainly better when I have a deadline, which is why this work suits me.&nbsp;

36
00:03:32,224 --> 00:03:36,142
Tutor: Yes, but it’s how you respond as that deadline approaches!

37
00:03:36,142 --> 00:03:40,063
[Q27答案句D： hide your emotion] Holly: I know I’ve got to look calm even if I’m in a panic.&nbsp;

38
00:03:40,063 --> 00:03:44,088
Tutor: Just think to yourself – no one must know I’m under pressure.

39
00:03:44,088 --> 00:03:47,942
Holly: Yeah – even though I’m multi-tasking like crazy!&nbsp;

40
00:03:47,942 --> 00:04:01,708
(Q28) [Q29答案句：think of all fine point =  focus on detail] Tutor: Another skill that events managers need is creativity. Often your client has what we call the ‘big picture’ idea, but it’s up to the events manager to 【think of all the fine points】 that go to making it work.

41
00:04:01,708 --> 00:04:07,808
Holly: Right, so I need to listen carefully to that idea and then fill in all the gaps.

42
00:04:07,808 --> 00:04:24,956
(Q29) Tutor: That’s right. And you’ll have a team working under you, so another key skill is leadership. Your team may have lots of ideas too, but you’ve got to make the ultimate choices. Do we have refreshments inside or out, for example?

43
00:04:24,956 --> 00:04:27,832
Holly: Isn’t it better to be democratic?&nbsp;

44
00:04:27,832 --> 00:04:40,844
[Q29答案句F： believe in what you ... =. trust your own views] Tutor: It’s a nice idea, but you have the ultimate responsibility. So, believe in what you think best. Be prepared to say ‘yes’, that’s a good idea but it won’t work here.

45
00:04:40,844 --> 00:04:43,164
Holly: I see what you mean.&nbsp;

46
00:04:43,164 --> 00:04:53,249
(Q30) Holly：What about the networking side of things? I know it’s an area that a lot of students worry about because we don’t have much experience to offer others.&nbsp;

47
00:04:53,249 --> 00:05:02,350
Tutor: But even without it – you can still be an interesting person with useful ideas. And the more people you impress, the better.

48
00:05:02,350 --> 00:05:05,592
Holly: I guess that will help me when I apply for a real job.&nbsp;

49
00:05:05,592 --> 00:05:11,573
[Q30答案句H: think ahead = thinking of the future] Tutor: Exactly – think ahead – remember what your ambitions are and keep them in mind.

50
00:05:11,573 --> 00:05:14,073
Holly: Definitely.&nbsp;

